---
layout: base.njk
---
{# data-pagefind-ignore: without it every placeholder is indexed (the stub
   sits inside base.njk's data-pagefind-body), so a narrowed edition's
   search for "archive" or "Fian Ilchruinne" returned dozens of identical
   "Not included in this edition" results. Real excluded titles never
   leaked - only this generic text - so this is de-noising, not privacy. #}
<article class="excluded-notice" data-pagefind-ignore>
  {% if edition.excludedNotice %}
  {# An edition's own plain-register notice (lib/editions.js). Deliberately
     NO cross-domain link: on the children's domain the reference site is
     the adult one, and a child cannot judge that link. Back goes to this
     domain's own /start/. #}
  <h1 class="page-title">{{ edition.excludedNotice.title }}</h1>
  <p class="page-intro">{{ edition.excludedNotice.intro }}</p>
  <p><a href="/star-rangers/start/">← {{ edition.excludedNotice.back }}</a></p>
  {% else %}
  {# Since 2026-10-09 the stub is a brief summary page with the onward link
     (Dermot's choice, after a site review read the stubs as dead ends): the
     page's own title and description, and a sentence saying which edition
     carries it. `excludedPage` is computed in .eleventy.js from the page's
     own file, because the computed title and description have already been
     replaced by the time the template runs. A paginated page has no file of
     its own and falls back to the generic heading. The carrying edition is
     named by tier: a tier-gated thread's pages point at the thread's home
     domain, everything else at the full record. Links to these stubs are
     un-linked in prose by the same change, so a reader arrives here only by
     a direct link, a search result or an outside site. #}
  {% set gated = excludedPage and excludedPage.tier and excludedPage.tier != "general" %}
  <h1 class="page-title">{{ excludedPage.title if excludedPage and excludedPage.title else "Not included in this edition" }}</h1>
  {% if excludedPage and excludedPage.description %}
  <p class="page-intro">{{ excludedPage.description }}</p>
  {% endif %}
  {# "Fian Ilchruinne" is deliberately hardcoded, NOT site.name: it names the
     record the onward link belongs to, and on a branded edition site.name is
     the local door's own brand. #}
  <p>
    {% if gated %}This page belongs to the {{ excludedPage.tier }} edition of <em>Fian Ilchruinne</em>, which this site does not carry.{% else %}This page is part of the full <em>Fian Ilchruinne</em> record, which this edition does not carry.{% endif %}
    Read it at <a href="https://{{ referenceDomain }}{{ page.url }}">{{ referenceDomain }}{{ page.url }}</a>.
  </p>
  <p><a href="/star-rangers/">← Back home</a></p>
  {% endif %}
</article>
